{"id":"79d221b15456acae02780e89a52cd269e82b4c192526901656b7e9dccd275054","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-10T12:12:27.894000481Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## What to build\n\nThe TUI filter, tag filter, sort and dashboard statistics call the lib's query module instead of reimplementing it. Saved views convert to a Filter in one place. Ticket statistics become a lib function used by both `ti stats` and the TUI dashboard. The Priority \"unprioritised ranks last\" rule exists once.\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI `/` filter is ASCII-only and searches title and description only, so it disagrees with `ti list --search` and with the glossary's Search (case-insensitive across all languages, scopes, Phrases, comments). The Priority ordering rule exists in three copies; tag filtering, saved-view conversion and stats aggregation are each duplicated between the TUI and the CLI.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test shows a Unicode, scoped or Phrase Search matching the same tickets in the TUI filter as in `ti list --search`\n- [ ] Only one implementation of the Priority ranking rule remains\n- [ ] Saved view → Filter conversion is written once\n- [ ] `ti stats` and the TUI dashboard share one stats function with a lib unit test\n- [ ] Existing list, stats and TUI tests pass; `--json` output is unchanged\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone — can start immediately.\n\n## Notes\n\nEnforces CONTEXT.md terms Search, Search scope, Phrase and Priority. Overlaps the closed-time work in the history ticket only for the \"closed in last 7 days\" figure; whichever lands second should reuse the first."}}}